A Hermitian matrix over $K/L$ of rank $\rho$ is congruent to $\operatorname{diag}(I_\rho,0)$: if $B\ne0$, the form $H(X)=X^{\mathsf T}B\bar X\in L$ is not identically zero, because $H(X+cY)=H(X)+c\bar cH(Y)+\operatorname{Tr}_{K/L}(\bar c\,X^{\mathsf T}B\bar Y)$ and the trace form of $K/L$ is nondegenerate; if $H(e)=a\ne0$, choose $c$ with $c\bar c=a^{-1}$, which exists since the norm $z\mapsto z^{2^h+1}$ maps the cyclic group $K^\times$ onto $L^\times$; then $H(ce)=1$, $K^N$ is the direct sum of $Kce$ and its orthogonal complement for $B$, and induction on $N$ applies.